  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: {"phase":"NO_VERIFIED_RESULT","availability":{"tablecheck:native-omakase-1":{"status":"AVAILABLE","receptionMode":"RESERVATION_SUPPORTED","checkedAt":"2026-08-19T07:20:00.000Z","evidenceIds":["evidence:restaurant:tablecheck-entity-match:ba1b28bcb8acf8b9fa0dfb71","evidence:restaurant:tablecheck-availability:ef27aaaec32cbc91035b4768"],"displayExpiresAt":"2026-08-19T07:30:00.000Z","freshnessPolicyVersion":"restaurant-availability-display-freshness@1","timeWindowCoverage":{"date":"2026-08-19","partySize":2,"requestedWindow":{"earliest":"19:00","latest":"19:00"},"covered":[{"earliest":"19:00","latest":"19:00","status":"AVAILABLE"}],"uncovered":[],"stopReason":"RESULT_FOUND"},"sourceAttempts":[{"source":"TABLECHECK","outcome":"AVAILABLE"}],"sourceProvider":"TABLECHECK","requestFingerprint":"{\"date\":\"2026-08-19\",\"timeWindow\":{\"earliest\":\"19:00\",\"latest\":\"19:00\"},\"partySize\":2}"}},"browserInputs":[{"objective":"Select the most specific observed public region/station entrance for the authoritative location. Follow observed links through region menus as needed, or fill the observed public location search using LOCATION. Reveal its public restaurant list; do not open restaurant details yet.","progress":"Follow an observed region entrance naming the requested area, continuing through a broader parent menu if necessary; observe its public results.","observation":{"targets":[{"ref":"observation:1:target:1","kind":"LINK","role":"link","label":"Shibuya","controlGroupLabel":"Unlabelled group","href":"https://tabelog.com/en/tokyo/A1303/A130301/rstLst/?sw=omakase","availableActions":["OPEN_LINK"]}],"pageActions":["WAIT"]},"skillSource":"# Tabelog Public Read\n\nUse only the supplied public Tabelog search and restaurant pages. Open only observed public links relevant to the stated objective: restaurant results, listing categories, query-filter removal, and result pagination. Treat challenge pages, external reservation providers, login, and booking paths as stop conditions; do not bypass a challenge or follow an external provider.\n\nCheckbox/range changes require an explicit source-owned query contract; GET form structure alone is not permission. When a public Tabelog availability surface has observed date and party controls, set only the authoritative values and re-observe before reading explicitly available time controls. Do not treat rankings, reviews, restaurant names, or prose times as identity or availability evidence.\n\nNever submit a reservation, enter personal details, or navigate outside the allowed Tabelog origin.\n\nOn an observed public listing search input, Discovery may fill only the supplied retrieval expression. Re-observe the current page and use an observed public query control or current result; never use the field to change the area, HARD criteria, date, party size, or time.\n\nWhen Discovery explicitly asks to broaden a sparse keyword query, choose a relevant category from the site's observed Search by category links and use its keyword-removal link if necessary. The observed `All` link in Search by category opens the category panel; use its permitted CLICK action, then re-observe the category choices. Do not guess that an unlabeled button opens this panel. Category links may preserve the old keyword. Keep the same area. A category is only a discovery lead; it does not establish that any restaurant satisfies a HARD criterion. Follow only an observed next-results link for pagination.\n\nThe source may label nonstandard calendar controls as `Date YYYY-MM-DD` and guest controls as `Guests N`. These labels are derived from the observed element, not the task goal. Use CLICK_AUTHORITATIVE with DATE or PARTY_SIZE for the exact requested value. Selected query controls and visible time choices alone do not establish bookable inventory.\n\nWait for a visible selectable date and an enabled visible guest control on the current calendar. Hidden future-month dates and disabled guest controls do not make the query ready. If the source reports that the current guest query cannot be adjusted, stop with a source-control limit; do not infer no availability for the requested date.\n\nThe observed English calendar time buttons navigate into booking forms. They are evidence-only; do not click them to inspect availability. Source-owned verification reads only captured public vacancy-query responses with matching merchant/date/party/time."},{"objective":"Apply the current public source search and reveal venue result cards for the authoritative area and retrieval terms. Do not submit a reservation.","progress":"The current source listing has not yet produced a parsed public venue result or an explicit empty result.","observation":{"targets":[{"ref":"observation:1:target:1","kind":"LINK","role":"link","label":"Stale venue","controlGroupLabel":"Unlabelled group","href":"https://www.tablecheck.com/en/stale-result","availableActions":["OPEN_LINK"]},{"ref":"observation:1:target:2","kind":"BUTTON","role":"button","label":"Show public venues","controlGroupLabel":"Unlabelled group","type":"button","availableActions":["CLICK"]},{"ref":"observation:1:target:3","inputName":"search_text","kind":"INPUT","role":"textbox","label":"search_text","controlGroupLabel":"Unlabelled group","value":"stale query","type":"search","availableActions":["FILL_AUTHORITATIVE:RETRIEVAL"]}],"pageActions":["WAIT"]},"skillSource":"# TableCheck Public Read\n\nStart from the supplied public TableCheck search or restaurant page. Search-result cards, restaurant Guide pages, and clearly read-only schedule controls may be inspected. Prefer a visible public restaurant result that corresponds to the supplied objective; do not use navigation, help, restaurateur, account, login, or booking-submission links.\n\nOn the public `/en/japan/search` page, an observed checkbox or range may be changed only when it is part of a GET search form and the source policy classifies it as a query filter. Update, reopen, and reset are read-only only when their observed control remains within that same public search surface; re-observe each post-condition. For availability, set only the authoritative date and party size through observed controls, then wait or re-observe until the latest page visibly reflects both. A current, source-permitted service-category radio with `SET_CHECKED` is also a query prerequisite when the page says a category must be chosen: select one only when the current public category text supports its relevance to the immutable HARD criteria, read back the single checked member, then wait for a new category-bound result. It is never a booking action, does not prove stock, and a category without that public relevance requires human help. Read only explicitly bookable time controls. Do not infer a slot from prose, a selected-looking control, or a successful browser operation.\n\nThe search bar can expose both a wrapper combobox and its nested native input. The wrapper is not a fill target; the nested input's placeholder or name identifies the field. During Discovery, fill that observed public input only with the supplied retrieval expression, then re-observe and use an observed read-only search control or current result. A public result card may cover its own link at the click center. Follow only the executor-checked, currently observed result URL and re-observe the restaurant page.\n\nNever submit a reservation, continue to login, enter contact details, or use a link outside the allowed TableCheck origin.\n\nA read-only Time control is a query control. The generic browser skill governs choosing native or custom observed options. Its options are query values, not evidence of stock. Reservation links remain observation-only. A result at a different mealtime cannot prove the requested window empty.\n\nAn observed reservation slot can use either `/en/shops/<same-slug>/reserve` or `/en/<same-slug>/reserve/landing`. Read it only when its slug is the current guide's same 